flowchart TB
  accTitle: Obsidian Research Agent architecture
  accDescr: An Obsidian desktop plugin. A mission starts in the console. The agent loop follows a durable mission plan, calls the model, and proposes actions, and every action passes the prepared-action gate, which shows an exact approval, records a receipt, and reads the result back. Sourced notes are written to the vault, and an interrupted run resumes from its plan. Web and scholarly search, Linear and GitHub, the code sandbox, and a local companion service are destinations behind the gate.

  subgraph obs["OBSIDIAN DESKTOP"]
    console["`**Mission console**
    chat, run details`"]
    loop["`**Agent loop**
    durable plan, lead + specialists`"]
    gate["`**Prepared-action gate**
    approval, receipt, readback`"]
    vault[("`**Vault**
    notes, runs, memory`")]
  end

  model["`**Model**
  Ollama Cloud or compatible`"]
  web["`**Web + scholarly search**`"]
  work["`**Linear + GitHub**`"]
  helpers["`**Local helpers** · opt-in
  code sandbox, companion service`"]

  console ==>|mission| loop
  loop ==>|every action| gate
  gate ==>|sourced notes| vault
  loop <-->|prompts, tool calls| model
  gate --> web
  gate -.-> work
  gate -.-> helpers

  classDef key fill:#e6eee9,stroke:#315e55,stroke-width:2.5px,color:#192c32
  classDef ext fill:#f7f8f5,stroke:#7c8f83,color:#192c32
  classDef side fill:#f7f8f5,stroke:#b6c3ba,stroke-dasharray:6 4,color:#526460
  class gate key
  class model,web,work ext
  class helpers side
